ARM: use interrupt-masked atomics when ARM_NO_EXCLUSIVES is set

Three places choose the LDREX/STREX implementation, and they do not all key off
the same thing:

  atomic.h  - one conditional on __LINUX_ARM_ARCH__ governs the whole file, and
              its #else branch is already pure C around raw_local_irq_save().

  bitops.h  - keys off CONFIG_SMP, not the architecture. Even a UP build sends a
              *variable* bit number to the ldrex/strex assembly form; only a
              compile-time-constant bit takes the C path. Half the bitops in the
              kernel would quietly never complete.

  cmpxchg.h - cannot simply fall back. Its pre-ARMv6 path uses swp/swpb, and
              ARMv7-M dropped SWP entirely, so that code will not even assemble
              here. Needs a real interrupt-masked implementation.

--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/atomic.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/atomic.h
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 #define arch_atomic_read(v)	READ_ONCE((v)->counter)
 #define arch_atomic_set(v,i)	WRITE_ONCE(((v)->counter), (i))
 
-#if __LINUX_ARM_ARCH__ >= 6
+#if __LINUX_ARM_ARCH__ >= 6 && !defined(CONFIG_ARM_NO_EXCLUSIVES)
 
